course: dictionary
lesson: 3554
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Felt» is a good example. «She felt happy when the bell rang.» Here felt is the past of feel, so it tells us how she was feeling.
explain: Now look at this: «The hat was made of thick grey felt.» Felt here is a thick, soft cloth made by pressing wool or other fibres together. Ask yourself: is this a feeling, or a thing you could touch and cut? That question solves it.
explain: A third meaning appears in «Felt-tip pens dry out without a cap.» The hyphen joins felt and tip to make one name: a pen with a soft tip made of this material. When you see felt next to another word, check whether they make a new phrase.
fact: «Felt» has three meanings: the past of «feel», a thick soft cloth, and part of «felt-tip pen».
fact: As the past of «feel», «felt» goes with feel, feels and feeling: I feel, she feels, I felt yesterday.
fact: Felt is a thick, soft cloth made by pressing wool or other fibres together.
fact: A felt-tip pen has a soft tip made of this material, and the ink inside soaks into the paper.
fact: You do not count felt the way you count pencils: you say a piece of felt, not two felts.
exercise: «She felt sorry for the lost puppy.» In this sentence, what does felt mean? | A thick, soft cloth | A pen with a soft tip | A kind of hat | *The past of feel, showing how she was feeling
exercise: Mia cut a star from red felt for her card. What is felt here? | The past of feel | A pen | *A thick, soft cloth made by pressing wool together | A sad feeling
exercise: Which phrase names a pen with a soft tip? | felt like | felt sorry | felt better | *felt-tip pen
test: «After the race, Sam felt better.» What does felt tell us? | *Sam was feeling better, the past of feel | Sam was made of felt | Sam wrote with a felt-tip pen | Sam was cut into a shape
test: Which sentence uses felt as a thick cloth? | «They felt sorry for him.» | «She felt much better today.» | *«The puppet was stuffed with grey felt.» | «He felt cold and tired.»
exam: In «Even the colours in black felt-tip ink can be pulled apart on wet kitchen paper», what does felt-tip mean? | The past of feel | A feeling of sadness | *Part of a pen name: a pen with a soft tip | A thick soft cloth
